{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"final","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MultipleColorSemanticToken","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["        \/\/ Assuming in Figma with have a color semantic token bgPrimary,","        \/\/ two semantic color tokens will be defined in Figma and generated by tokenator.","        \/\/ They can be declared in protocol ColorSemanticTokens,","        \/\/ and defined automaticaly in MISOTheme+ColorSemanticTokens extension","        var bgPrimaryLight: ColorSemanticToken { ColorRawTokens.functionalWhite }","        var bgPrimaryDark: ColorSemanticToken { ColorRawTokens.functionalDarkGray880 }","","        \/\/ Then the develoment team declares an \"higher\" level color semantic token for bgPrimary","        \/\/ inside ColorMultipleSemanticTokens protocol,","        \/\/ and defined inside MISOTheme+ColorMultipleSemanticToken extension","        var bgPrimary: MultipleColorSemanticToken { MultipleColorSemanticToken(light: bgPrimaryLight, dark: bgPrimaryDark) }","","        \/\/ If the same color is used whatever the color scheme is","        var bgPrimary: MultipleColorSemanticToken { MultipleColorSemanticToken(bgPrimaryLight) }","","        \/\/ The theme exposes both generated color semantic tokens and \"crafted\" higher level color semantic tokens.","        \/\/ It is recommended to use the higher level version as it is less error-prone."],"type":"codeListing"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["     @Environment(\\.theme) var theme","     @Environment(\\.colorScheme) var colorScheme","","    \/\/ Given you want to apply the color token \"surfaceBrandPrimary\"","    var body: some View {","        \/\/ Apply the token of color for the view without managing yourself the color scheme","        SomeView()","            .background(theme.colors.surfaceBrandPrimary)","","        \/\/ Or also foregroundStyle(), foregroundColor(), accentColor(), ...","    }"],"type":"codeListing"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["    \/\/ Or get the token depending to the color scheme and do whatever you want with","    theme.colors.surfaceBrandPrimary.color(for: colorScheme)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"name":"Since","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"OUDS 0.8.0","type":"text"}]}],"style":"note","type":"aside"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MultipleColorSemanticToken","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Class","modules":[{"name":"Tokens for semantics"}],"title":"MultipleColorSemanticToken","externalID":"c:@M@MISOTokensSemantic@objc(cs)MultipleColorSemanticToken","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MultipleColorSemanticToken","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"class"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Inherits From","type":"inheritsFrom","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MISOTokensSemantic\/objc(cs)NSObject"],"kind":"relationships"},{"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MISOTokensSemantic\/objc(pl)NSObject","doc:\/\/MISOTokensSemantic\/s7CVarArgP","doc:\/\/MISOTokensSemantic\/s28CustomDebugStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/MISOTokensSemantic\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/MISOTokensSemantic\/SQ","doc:\/\/MISOTokensSemantic\/SH","doc:\/\/MISOTokensSemantic\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/MISOTokensSemantic\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/MISOTokensSemantic\/documentation\/MISOTokensSemantic\/MultipleColorSemanticToken","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/misotokenssemantic\/multiplecolorsemantictoken"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/MISOTok